---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GEOQuickAnswer from '../components/GEOQuickAnswer.astro';
import FAQSection from '../components/FAQSection.astro';

const pageTitle = 'What is Destroy Website? The Web Demolition Game Explained';
const pageDescription = 'What is Destroy Website? Learn all about the viral browser physics game, how client-side DOM demolition works, and why it is 100% legal, safe, and harmless.';

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'What is Destroy Website? The Complete Guide to Browser Web Destruction',
    description: 'A comprehensive technical and gameplay breakdown of Destroy Website, its 2D physics sandbox engine, and security guarantees.',
    author: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'Destroy Website Team',
      url: 'https://destroywebsite.com',
    },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'Destroy Website',
      logo: {
        '@type': 'ImageObject',
        url: 'https://destroywebsite.com/og-image.jpg',
      },
    },
    datePublished: '2026-08-01',
    dateModified: '2026-10-02',
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://destroywebsite.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'What is Destroy Website', item: 'https://destroywebsite.com/what-is-destroy-website/' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={schemas}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-12 space-y-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-destruct-dim" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-neon-cyan">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-white">What is Destroy Website</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center space-y-3">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">
        What is <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-neon-pink to-neon-cyan">Destroy Website</span>?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-destruct-muted max-w-xl mx-auto">
        The viral browser physics phenomenon turning stressful webpages into shatterable playgrounds.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- GEO Quick Summary -->
    <GEOQuickAnswer
      question="Summary: How does Destroy Website work?"
      directAnswer="Destroy Website is a 100% harmless, client-side browser game where players enter a URL to generate a virtual physical clone of the webpage. Using 8 interactive weapons, players can crack, burn, or blast away HTML elements. The actual web server and database remain untouched."
      bulletPoints={[
        'Client-Side Only: Runs within an isolated HTML5 Canvas in your browser.',
        'Zero Server Harm: Does not ping, flood, or alter target servers.',
        'Anti-Stress Purpose: Designed purely for fun, relaxation, and comedy.',
        'No Downloads Required: Works instantly across PC, Mac, and mobile.',
      ]}
    />

    <!-- Main Content Article -->
    <article class="bg-arcade-card border border-arcade-border rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-destruct-text">
      <!-- Section 1: The Viral Phenomenon -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-arcade-border pb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🚀</span>
          <span>The Viral Phenomenon: TikTok, YouTube Shorts & Reddit Explosion</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-destruct-muted">
          If you recently saw a 10-second viral clip on TikTok, YouTube Shorts, or Reddit where someone typed in their <strong>school portal, former employer's homepage, or Wikipedia</strong> and blasted it to smithereens with a rocket launcher or laser cannon — welcome to <strong>Destroy Website</strong> (hosted at <a href="https://destroywebsite.com" class="text-neon-cyan font-bold underline">destroywebsite.com</a>).
        </p>
        <p class="text-destruct-muted">
          Content creators love recording fast-paced, high-satisfaction screen captures of taking down massive web portals. When a single short video amasses millions of views, hundreds of thousands of gamers immediately rush to search <em>"destroy website"</em> or <em>"destroy any website"</em> to try it themselves.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Historical Lineage -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-arcade-border pb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>👑</span>
          <span>Why Anti-Stress & Destruction Games are Timeless Classics</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-destruct-muted">
          Digital destruction has always been one of the most beloved and enduring game genres in internet history:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-destruct-muted list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>NetDisaster (Early 2000s):</strong> The legendary pioneer that let users summon virtual UFOs, meteors, and coffee spills on websites.</li>
          <li><strong>Desktop Destroyer:</strong> The classic desktop app where players used hammers, buzzsaws, and flamethrowers to smash their monitor screens.</li>
          <li><strong>KickAss Asteroids:</strong> The viral JavaScript bookmarklet that turned any webpage into a playable Asteroids space battlefield.</li>
          <li><strong>Kick the Buddy:</strong> The multi-million download mobile gaming sensation proving that interactive stress relief is universally popular.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-destruct-muted">
          <strong>Destroy Website</strong> brings this heritage into the modern web era: powered by pure <strong>HTML5 Canvas and 2D physics simulation</strong>, there are no browser extensions, Flash plugins, or downloads required. You open the page, and within <strong>0.1 seconds</strong>, you are in the cockpit of demolition.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Embedded Image Banner -->
      <figure class="my-6 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border-2 border-neon-pink/40 shadow-[0_0_25px_rgba(255,42,109,0.2)]">
        <img
          src="/images/hero-banner.jpg"
          alt="Destroy Website 2D Arcade Web Demolition Sandbox"
          width="1200"
          height="675"
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="p-3 bg-arcade-darkest text-xs text-center text-destruct-dim font-mono">
          Figure 1: Cyberpunk arcade destruction arena on Destroy Website.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-arcade-border pb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🛡️</span>
          <span>Is Destroy Website Legal and Safe? (Debunking Myths)</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-2.5 text-destruct-muted">
          <p>
            <strong>Myth 1: "Is this a DDoS or hacking tool?"</strong><br />
            <span class="text-neon-green font-bold">Reality: No.</span> Destroy Website never sends malicious packets, flood requests, or unauthorized commands to any server. It is purely a visual simulation that creates a local screenshot or DOM blueprint.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Myth 2: "Can the website owner see that I destroyed their page?"</strong><br />
            <span class="text-neon-green font-bold">Reality: No.</span> All physics calculations and pixel changes occur exclusively in your local machine's GPU and RAM. The real website remains completely unmodified.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Myth 3: "Do I need to install any suspicious files or extensions?"</strong><br />
            <span class="text-neon-green font-bold">Reality: No.</span> The entire sandbox runs inside standard HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript without requiring any software installation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white border-b border-arcade-border pb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⚙️</span>
          <span>Technical Physics Architecture</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-destruct-muted">
          When a webpage is loaded into the sandbox:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-destruct-muted">
          <li><strong>DOM Parsing:</strong> The layout structure is converted into bounding boxes representing headers, buttons, cards, and paragraphs.</li>
          <li><strong>Rigid-Body Mapping:</strong> Each bounding box receives mass, friction, restitution (bounciness), and health points.</li>
          <li><strong>Impulse Mechanics:</strong> Weapons apply directional kinetic force vectors and particle spawns based on distance from the impact center.</li>
          <li><strong>Destruction Meter:</strong> The engine continuously calculates the percentage of eliminated nodes until reaching 100% total annihilation.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </article>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion -->
    <FAQSection />
  </div>
</Layout>
